"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[46833],{946833:n=>{n.exports="# Table Calculation to Window Measure Migration\n\n## Supported Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Percent of Total\n\n**Tableau:** `SUM([x]) / TOTAL(SUM([x]))`\n\n**Metric View:** Three measures -- base, grand total (window), composed division.\n\n```yaml\nmeasures:\n  # 1. Base measure (may already exist)\n  - name: total_abandons\n    expr: SUM(abandons_)\n\n  # 2. Grand total window measure\n  - name: grand_total_abandons\n    expr: SUM(abandons_)\n    window:\n      - order: main_date\n        range: all\n        semiadditive: last\n\n  # 3. Composed percent-of-total\n  - name: abandons_distribution\n    expr: MEASURE(total_abandons) / MEASURE(grand_total_abandons)\n    display_name: 'Q/Abands Dist'\n    format:\n      type: percentage\n```\n\n**Why this works:** `range: all` aggregates across all rows regardless of ordering, equivalent to Tableau's `TOTAL()` which sums across the entire partition. The composed measure uses `MEASURE()` division which is safe (div-by-zero returns NULL).\n\n### Pattern 2: Standalone TOTAL\n\n**Tableau:** `TOTAL(SUM([x]))`\n\n**Metric View:** Single window measure with `range: all`.\n\n```yaml\nmeasures:\n  - name: grand_total_revenue\n    expr: SUM(revenue)\n    display_name: 'Row Sum CF'\n    window:\n      - order: order_date\n        range: all\n        semiadditive: last\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Running Sum\n\n**Tableau:** `RUNNING_SUM(SUM([x]))`\n\n**Metric View:** Window measure with `range: cumulative`.\n\n```yaml\nmeasures:\n  - name: cumulative_activations\n    expr: SUM(assumedactives)\n    display_name: 'Cumulative Activations'\n    window:\n      - order: activation_date\n        range: cumulative\n        semiadditive: last\n```\n\n**Why this works:** `range: cumulative` computes the running aggregate up to the current ordering value, equivalent to `RUNNING_SUM()` which computes the cumulative sum along the partition.\n\n## Ordering Dimension Selection\n\n### For TOTAL (range: all)\n\n- Ordering dimension is irrelevant for aggregation (all rows included regardless)\n- Use the first time-based dimension available (date, month, etc.)\n- If no time dimension, use any dimension from the rows shelf\n- **The choice does not affect correctness** -- only the semiadditive behavior when the order dimension is not in GROUP BY\n\n### For RUNNING_SUM (range: cumulative)\n\n- Ordering dimension determines accumulation axis -- MUST be correct\n- Inspect the calc's table-calc spec in the XML (`<table-calculation>` under the calculation, attribute `ordering-type`):\n  - `ordering-type=\"Rows\"` -> first dimension on the worksheet's rows shelf\n  - `ordering-type=\"Columns\"` -> first dimension on the worksheet's columns shelf\n- Prefer time-based dimensions (date, month, week) when available\n- **Fail-safe:** If ordering dimension cannot be determined, SKIP the calc\n\n## Naming Convention\n\n- Grand total measures: prefix with `grand_total_` (e.g., `grand_total_abandons`)\n- Cumulative measures: prefix with `cumulative_` (e.g., `cumulative_activations`)\n- Distribution/composed measures: suffix with `_distribution` or use original Tableau caption normalized\n- Base measures: derived from original Tableau caption (existing convention)\n\n**Important:** Ensure no name collisions with existing measures or source columns. Measure names MUST differ from source column names to avoid `[UNRESOLVED_COLUMN]` errors.\n\n## Window Measure Spec and MEASURE() Rules\n\nWindow measure YAML syntax (`window`, `order`, `range`, `semiadditive`) and `MEASURE()` composition rules are documented in the `using-metric-views` skill. Migration only uses two ranges: `range: all` (for TOTAL) and `range: cumulative` (for RUNNING_SUM). For the MEASURE() arithmetic-only constraint, see \"Division Safety and MEASURE() Constraints\" in `calc_to_sql.md`.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n### Duplicate Base Measures\n\nIf the workbook already has `total_abandons: SUM(abandons_)` as a regular measure:\n\n- Reuse the existing measure for the base\n- Only add the `grand_total_` variant as a new window measure\n- Use the existing measure name in the composed division\n\n### Multiple Worksheets Using Same Calc\n\nFor TOTAL (`range: all`): Pick ordering dimension from ANY worksheet -- no conflict.\nFor RUNNING_SUM: Use the first worksheet found.\n\n### Nested Table Calcs\n\n```\nTOTAL(SUM([Calc_A]))  where Calc_A = SUM([x]) / SUM([y])\n```\n\nIf inner calc is a regular aggregate ratio, convert it first, then apply the TOTAL window on top. If nesting involves non-migratable TC functions, skip the entire expression.\n"}}]);
